  "text": "Inside the pad, alternating current flows through this coil. Watch the current reverse direction. That makes the magnetic field expand and collapse. Now place a second coil inside that changing field. The field induces a voltage in the second coil. The coils do not touch. They are magnetically linked. The phone then rectifies and regulates that power for its battery. Move the coils apart or off-center. Less of the field links them, so the transfer weakens and wastes energy. Wireless charging is energy crossing a changing magnetic field between two coils.",
